{"content":[{"c":["KIR"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Mesopotamian city from which the Syrians migrated to Damascus and back to which they were later exiled by the Assyrians (",{"href":"?bref=Amos.1.5","r":"Amos.1.5","rawR":"Amos.1.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Amos.1.5","value":"Amos.1.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Am 1:5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Amos.9.7","r":"Amos.9.7","rawR":"Amos.9.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Amos.9.7","value":"Amos.9.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:7"},"). Escape from Kir to Aram paralleled the exodus of the Israelites. It must have been a terribly bitter experience to have been deported (by Tiglath-pileser) back to Kir (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.16.9","r":"2Kgs.16.9","rawR":"2Kgs.16.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.16.9","value":"2Kgs.16.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 16:9"},"). Whether the city actually existed or not is debatable. It could have become a metaphor for enslavement and exile."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Fortress usually identified with the ancient capital of Moab. Soldiers from Kir were associated with those from Elam (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.22.6","r":"Isa.22.6","rawR":"Isa.22.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.22.6","value":"Isa.22.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 22:6"},"). Likewise, Kir was paralleled with Ar in Isaiah’s lament over Moab (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.15.1","r":"Isa.15.1","rawR":"Isa.15.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.15.1","value":"Isa.15.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"15:1"},"). Kir of Moab, therefore, is probably the same as Kir-hareseth (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.3.25","r":"2Kgs.3.25","rawR":"2Kgs.3.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.3.25","value":"2Kgs.3.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 3:25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.16.7","r":"Isa.16.7","rawR":"Isa.16.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.16.7","value":"Isa.16.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 16:7"},"), located at Kerak, 11 miles (17.7 kilometers) east of the southern end of the Dead Sea."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Kir","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Am 1:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Amos.1.5","rawQueryValue":"Amos.1.5","sourceRefExact":"Amos.1.5"},{"anchorText":"9:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Amos.9.7","rawQueryValue":"Amos.9.7","sourceRefExact":"Amos.9.7"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 16:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.16.9","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.16.9","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.16.9"},{"anchorText":"Is 22:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.22.6","rawQueryValue":"Isa.22.6","sourceRefExact":"Isa.22.6"},{"anchorText":"15:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.15.1","rawQueryValue":"Isa.15.1","sourceRefExact":"Isa.15.1"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 3:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.3.25","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.3.25","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.3.25"},{"anchorText":"Is 16:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.16.7","rawQueryValue":"Isa.16.7","sourceRefExact":"Isa.16.7"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"99467b75085d2c3c3377e819c888f21eb4aff9b8b85a74f32464ec19ce7163ce","sourceItemName":"Kir","sourceItemOrder":92,"sourceMember":"Articles/K.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Kir","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Kir","title":"Kir","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}